WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.202
-Our first guest tonight is an
Emmy Award-winning co-host of

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:06.172
"CBS Mornings,"
host of the SiriusXM show

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.873
"Gayle King in the House,"

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:10.509
and the editor at large of
"Oprah Daily."

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:13.245
The winter issue of
"O Quarterly," which features

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:15.882
this year's list of Oprah's
favorite things is on newsstands

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.583
now and available at
oprahdaily.com.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:18.584
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.353
our friend Gayle King,
everybody.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.455
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:31.497 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:40.573 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.676
Welcome back, Gayle.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.412
-Hello, human beings.
I'm so glad to be here.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:47.980
-It's nice to be in a room
with human beings, isn't it?

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.450
-It really is.
-It really is.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.218
-I do not take it for granted
ever.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.452
-Yes.
-Ever.

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:54.888
-Now more than ever.
-Ever, ever have.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.889
-This must have been, you know,
an exciting month for you.

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:58.958
We've talked about our shared

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.860
affection and appreciation
for Taylor Swift.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.861
-Yes.
-A big Taylor Swift month.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.196
-She has a new tour coming out.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.364
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.499
She has a new tour coming out.
-Be honest.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.968
When someone like her goes on
tour, do you have, like, an in

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.403
on tickets, or are you
on TicketM--

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.038
are you, like,
refreshing the link?

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:14.207
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.475
-I'm refreshing the link.
-There you go. Thank you.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.310
-No. I've been to all
of Taylor's concerts.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.347
And last time I was here,
she was coming the day after,

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.015
and I was so bummed.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:25.018
-Because I've seen her
in concert several times.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:27.820
And now the new -- the new
album, "Midnight at 3:00 a.m.,"

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.255
I got the deluxe version.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.589
-Oh, look at you.
-Yep.

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:33.059
She's going to be in New York
the 26th, 27th, 28th,

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.727
but I'm not sure.
-Yeah.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.062
-It's Memorial Day weekend.
-That's very exciting.

00:01:37.062 --> 00:01:38.264
-Oh, I'm definitely going.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.400
-A little creepy how much
you know it.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.201
-Oh, I'm definitely going.
-Alright, good.

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:44.837
That's very exciting.
-She is such a great songwriter.

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:45.838
I really like her.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:47.607
I like her music,
so I'm excited.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:50.043
-Of course. We talked about
your grandson, Luca.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.244
-Oh, yes.
-Just turned one.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.412
Look at this dude.
-Look, he just turned one.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.713
[ Audience aws ]

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.248
-Is he a Halloween minion
or is he an everyday minion?

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.150
-He was a minion, yes.
-He was a minion for Halloween.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.285
-Yes. And let -- He's very close

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.753
in age to your favorite
daughter, Addie.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.887
-Yeah.
-You only have one daughter.

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:02.688
-Yeah, we have one.
She is my favorite.

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:04.323
-He was born on the 13th.

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:05.491
-She was born on the 15th.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.192
-Yes, so that's why I always
remember that.

00:02:07.192 --> 00:02:10.429
-And I want to ask a question
because the last time

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:12.298
you were here, we talked
about -- you know,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.134
it's a very high-stakes
operation when you decide what

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.803
your grandchildren are going
to call you as a grandparent.

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.472
-And Seth threw shade, guys.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.973
-He threw shade.

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:23.343
-'Cause you wanted --
Now, it should be noted, I --

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:26.512
It is confirmed that I'm
on Oprah's side here.

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:27.780
-Yes.
-Oprah also threw shade.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.881
-Yes, yes, yes. Yeah.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:30.717
-That you wanted to be called
"Gaya."

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.352
-I ignore her shade.
And her shade is private.

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.622
Your shade was in front of
all of the studio audience.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.089
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:38.224
And that night when I got home,

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.792
people go,
"Well, maybe he has a point."

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.527
-Yeah.
-I did say I wanted to be called

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.930
"Gaya" because it kind of sounds
like Gayle.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.731
-Uh-uh.
-And it means "mother Earth."

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:48.000
And Seth said, "If you have
to explain a grandma name,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.368
that's probably not
a good idea."

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.270
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.640
-So we're a year in.
What does Luca call you?

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.642
-Well, he's not really
speaking yet,

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:56.709
so I'm going to leave it up
to him.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.244
But I've come up with
another name.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.112
"Gan-Gan."
-"Gan-Gan?"

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:02.482
[ Audience aws ]
-Isn't that nice? Gan-Gan?

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.317
[ Applause ]

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.185
-You're all missing the point.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.820
-Seth, I think that's --
-It's up to Luca.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.255
-I know.
-Just wait.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.591
-Yeah, but don't you want to
just sort of guide him along?

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.325
I don't want him
to call me Gayle.

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:15.995
Ellen DeGeneres said he can just
call you, "Hey, Miss Lady."

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.630
I don't like that.
-Yeah. No. That's true.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.732
-I want something that's
friendly and cute.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.268
-Gan-Gan's not the worst.
It's better than Gaya. Yeah.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.903
-See, I thought Gaya was nice,

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:26.005
but now you have me
rethinking myself.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.240
-I'm sorry that I --
-I don't like doubting myself.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.277
-I'm being a real bully
about this, and I apologize.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:34.847
So more importantly,
midterms are tomorrow.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.882
-Yes.
-What's your day like?

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.550
Obviously, stakes are very high.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.419
You're in the news business.
-Stakes are very high.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:44.056
-I do feel like maybe your
Wednesday morning will be more,

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.258
I mean, tomorrow when you're
on in the morning,

00:03:46.258 --> 00:03:48.127
certainly, you won't have much
to say other than the fact

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.195
that people are going to
the polls.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.529
-It's going to be
a very long day.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:53.266
And also, when I was coming
here, in the elevator,

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.467
somebody on your team said,

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.169
"Seth gives us a day off
so we can vote."

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.536
So, bravo to you.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.536 --> 00:03:58.437
-I think that's great.
It's great.

00:03:58.437 --> 00:03:59.571
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:59.571 --> 00:04:02.041
-No, that is --
-No. No, no, seriously.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.075
-It's not -- it's --
-Seriously, Seth --

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:05.678
-I have to stop you.
It's not true.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.413
-No, it is true.
-No, it's not true.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.615
Yes, they have the day off,
and I hope they all vote.

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:12.284
But NBC was like,
"We want to put the news on."

00:04:12.284 --> 00:04:14.353
-No. They said it was Seth.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:17.123
-No, they did -- I just don't
want to be out here being like,

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:20.593
"I went into NBC and I was like,
'You listen to me.'"

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.128
And they're like,
"Why are you here?"

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:24.463
-Okay.
Well, your team has the day off

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:26.565
and the woman told me
that she's going to be voting.

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:27.933
And I just thought
that was very cool.

00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:29.635
-I certainly hope they all vote.
-Yes, I do too.

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:31.337
-And if they don't show me
the sticker,

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:32.905
they go into the penalty box.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.874
[ Laughter ]
-I do too. I do too.

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:37.142
I can't wait to vote,
but I'm very nervous.

00:04:37.142 --> 00:04:39.545
It's going to be a long day.
-When you cover it --

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.913
-It's going to be
a long, long day.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.448
-You know what?
I do, again, I think like --

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.316
Even on Wednesday morning,
there's a real likelihood that

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:46.218
a lot of these bigger elections

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:47.420
are going to be
so close to call.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.588
-That's true.
-And we do live in an era now

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:52.758
where I feel like conspiracy
theorists often reflect

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:55.461
back to the first thing
that is said about the results

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.929
from people
in the news business.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:57.796
-Yeah, people are
highly suspicious.

00:04:57.796 --> 00:04:59.031
-So, how do you speak about it?

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:00.466
-They're very suspicious.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.801
And listen, by the end of
the day tomorrow, there will be

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.369
several races
that you don't know.

00:05:04.369 --> 00:05:07.540
Last time, the last election,
we were on the air --

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.808
I didn't even get to go home.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:11.243
I ended up wearing the same
dress that I started out

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:13.712
in the morning, when we started,
to the next day

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:15.414
because the races went so long.

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.616
This time, I think they're going
to break it up a little bit.

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:19.118
But we may still not know.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.654
And just because you don't know
doesn't mean

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.188
there's something wrong
with the process.

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:26.825
But it's so scary to me, Seth,
because people are so --

00:05:26.825 --> 00:05:29.061
they're so doubtful.

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:31.764
There's such mistrust
that it's frightening to me.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:34.366
-It is a very frightening time.
-Yes.

00:05:34.366 --> 00:05:36.335
-I was looking at
your monologue.

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:39.171
-We're going to have to face it
no matter what, but I think one

00:05:39.171 --> 00:05:42.274
of the nice things is
there are the holidays coming.

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:43.609
They are Oprah's favorite thing.
-Yeah.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.444
-We're going to talk about it in
our next act,

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:47.413
but I wanted to start with
a ritual to kick it off.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.181
-Yes, yes, yes.
-I have some chai tea,

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:51.016
which I know this is --
-That's her favorite. Yes.

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:52.551
-This is an Oprah staple.

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:54.753
And I'm going to pour us
some chai tea.

00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:57.189
And what do you -- You have
some affirmations for us?

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:59.491
-Okay, now this is good. This is
on her favorite things list.

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:01.060
I like this.
-Okay.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.995
-And, Seth, we're going to do
this together.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.464
-Okay. Gotcha.
-Because what do you do,

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:06.065
Seth Meyers, to center yourself?

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:08.534
-What do I do to center myself?
-Yes. What do you do?

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.269
-I don't feel particularly
centered if I'm being honest.

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:11.870
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.639
May I have a suggestion for you?
-Yes. Great.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.075
-This is "The Life You Want"
daily inspiration cards.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.976
Oprah is really, guys,
a quote a minute.

00:06:17.976 --> 00:06:19.278
She's very good.
-Yeah.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.980
-So, we have Oprah
and other thought leaders.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.649
And so every day there are
365 cards in this box.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.884
-Okay. That's one for every day.
-Yeah, one for every day.

00:06:25.884 --> 00:06:28.020
[ Laughter ]
So, she takes a card.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.123
She reads a card while she's
sipping her chai tea.

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:34.326
-So, she reads a quote that she
of -- one of her quotes?

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:35.828
[ Laughter ]
-No, no. This is for you.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.629
-Oh, this is for me.
-This is for you.

00:06:37.629 --> 00:06:40.599
-But should I give 365 quotes
for Oprah?

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:42.267
-For her, she's just
sipping the chai.

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:43.602
-Oh, I see.
-For you.

00:06:43.602 --> 00:06:45.104
-For me, it's like I have her
there with me sipping.

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:46.538
-Yes. Yes, yes.
-Okay.

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:47.873
-Yeah, you can feel
her presence.

00:06:47.873 --> 00:06:49.708
So, one of the cards says this.

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:52.244
Very appropriate the night
before election.

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:54.780
"Transformation doesn't happen
unless you're willing.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.549
It's your choice."
-Mm.

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:57.750
-So that's on the front
of the card.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.952
Then the back,
something to think about.

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.086
Then she has, you know,

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:03.122
breathing exercises,
meditative things.

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:04.623
I like that.
-Okay. Great.

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:06.425
-Would you like to pick a card?
-I would love to pick a card.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:07.559
-Pick a card, any card.

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:08.794
-Okay, I feel like
you forced that card.

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:11.297
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:12.265
-No, I didn't.
I have three to choose from.

00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:13.799
-Okay, ready?
-Yes.

00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:16.101
-Gaya is a perfectly appropriate
name.

00:07:16.101 --> 00:07:20.039
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:22.241
No, that's not it.
-Don't try to clean it up.

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:24.276
-Alright, so I start here.
This is an Oprah quote.

00:07:24.276 --> 00:07:26.045
"Your life is always
speaking to you.

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:27.980
The fundamental question is,
'Will you listen?'"

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.815
Mm, chai.
-How about that?

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:32.385
[ Laughter ]
Okay, I'll take another sip.

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.619
-And then something
to think about.

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:35.253
We all have that little voice
inside of us.

00:07:35.253 --> 00:07:36.655
That feeling...
-That is true.

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:38.157
-...deep in your gut that's
always there to give you --

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:39.658
By the way, at this point
in the card,

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:41.160
my kids are already screaming.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.461
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.461 --> 00:07:43.629
And I'll be like, "You be quiet!

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:46.632
Oprah is communicating with me
via card!"

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.368
What is whispering to you
right now?

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:52.271
-But these are 365 days that you
can pick something.

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:53.539
-It's lovely.
-It's just something --

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.207
I do think it's lovely. I do.
-Give me one more.

00:07:55.207 --> 00:07:56.675
I feel like you're --
-This is my last one.

00:07:56.675 --> 00:07:58.009
This is my last one.

00:07:58.009 --> 00:08:00.646
"Everything you do and say shows
the world who you are."

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:01.914
I know that's true.
-Mm-hmm.

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:03.282
-So who are you, Seth Meyers?

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.516
-Who am I?
-Who are you?

00:08:04.516 --> 00:08:06.084
-I'm someone who's regretting
how hard

00:08:06.084 --> 00:08:07.587
I've been on you
about this name.

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:09.421
-No, you don't care.
-I don't care at all.

00:08:09.421 --> 00:08:11.457
-I know you don't care.
I know you don't.

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:12.758
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:14.793
-Now we're going to do
some real -- some more.

00:08:14.793 --> 00:08:15.995
This is just one of many.

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:17.163
-Oh, I did bring some more
favorites for you.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:18.597
But this is something
that's on the list.

00:08:18.597 --> 00:08:19.898
-Alright. That's on the list.

00:08:19.898 --> 00:08:21.467
And we're going to see a bunch
more things on the list.

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:23.703
We'll be right back with
more from Gayle King.

